# {{ mod_name }}

A Galaxy on Fire 2 PC custom-content starter by {{ author_name }}.

Generate into `{{ mod_id | snake_case }}` and copy the folder to:

```text
<Galaxy on Fire 2>/mods/{{ mod_id | snake_case }}/
```

`init.lua` creates a system, two stations, an item, and a blueprint during
`EarlyInit`, then unlocks the blueprint once gameplay is active. Adjust IDs,
coordinates, factions, item balance, and ingredients before release.

The `assets` directory contains integration guidance only. Add assets you have
the right to distribute, then enable the commented texture/sprite code.

Open the generated folder in Visual Studio Code and install its recommended
Lua extension for ModAPI globals, item and asset table types, signatures, and
hover documentation. See `MODAPI-DEVELOPMENT.md`.

The generated Lua source is GPL-3.0-only. Klonker does not install, execute,
or manage the mod after generation.
